      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual message as a moral agent",
      "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the textual message, which frames the viewer as someone who must confront the moral responsibility implied by the text. The text 'it happened because of people who were 'just doing their jobs'' invites the user to identify with the collective of ordinary people who followed orders, suggesting a passive or complicit stance. This projection is not deictic (e.g., 'you') but is implied through the rhetorical structure that positions the viewer as part of the 'people' being discussed, encouraging self-reflection on complicity.",
